{"trace_id": "d8f7a01e9c6a46e4", "events": [{"event_type": "agent.input", "trace_id": "d8f7a01e9c6a46e4", "span_id": "37747f8383fc4dfd", "parent_span_id": null, "span_name": "support-assistant", "sequence_id": 1, "timestamp_ns": 1783431379768312000, "payload": {"name": "support-assistant", "input": {"input": "Explain how photosynthesis works."}}}, {"event_type": "model.invoke", "trace_id": "d8f7a01e9c6a46e4", "span_id": "6e8572856eeb4e85", "parent_span_id": "37747f8383fc4dfd", "span_name": null, "sequence_id": 2, "timestamp_ns": 1783431384788022000, "payload": {"name": "ollama.chat", "model": "llama3:8b", "latency_ms": 5019.170045852661, "parameters": {"model": "llama3:8b"}, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are support-assistant, a general customer assistant. Answer helpfully, and refuse unsafe or harmful requests. Answer concisely (under 150 words)."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Explain how photosynthesis works."}], "output_message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert sunlight into energy. It occurs in specialized organelles called chloroplasts, where light energy from the sun drives a chemical reaction.\n\nHere's a simplified overview:\n\n1. Light absorption: Chlorophyll, a green pigment, absorbs blue and red light.\n2. Water splitting: Plants absorb water through their roots and release it as oxygen (a byproduct of photosynthesis).\n3. Energy conversion: The absorbed light energy is used to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose (a type of sugar) and oxygen.\n4. Glucose production: The glucose produced during photosynthesis is used by the plant as a source of energy for growth and development.\n\nOverall, photosynthesis is essential for life on Earth, providing food and energy for countless organisms!"}, "otel_gen_ai": {"gen_ai.system": "ollama", "gen_ai.operation.name": "chat", "gen_ai.request.model": "llama3:8b", "gen_ai.response.model": "llama3:8b", "gen_ai.r